 "notes": "Source image: output/ranked-bases-2026-10-24/Screenshot 2026-10-24 130209.png. User-provided real TH16 ranked-base screenshot from a YouTube video. No source video URL was supplied. This is screenshot digitization, not real-game simulation calibration. Projection: screen_x = 996 + (x-y)*17.15; screen_y = 60 + (x+y)*12.83; village 44x44; x runs down-right, y down-left; building coordinates are top tiles. Wall caps were reviewed approximately 24 pixels above their ground centers. Params are also in grid.json. Wall workflow: ran tools/baselab/digitize.py walls (294 candidates), inspected projected overlays and rectified crops, then hand-traced visible wall runs and isolated posts. Final 323 wall tiles, with no walls removed under buildings during the final build. wall-paths.json records the hand edits. 94 visible buildings. All TH16 non-Tesla inventory counts match; 0/5 Hidden Teslas. No traps were imputed. Repeated Gold Mine, Elixir Collector, Gold Storage, Multi-Archer Tower and Builder Hut sprites were compared using local pixel templates to refine relative tile translations. Modes: all three Inferno Towers are multi, based on multiple emitter heads. X-Bows at (5,18), (14,8), (23,36) are both; the flat lower inside X-Bow at (33,27) is ground. Spell Towers: rage at (23,18), poison at (36,7). Cannon (6,32) and Mortar (0,33) show geared barrels. Crafting Station is Hot Candle (candle mode). Defending CC panel: x1 Inferno Dragon, x1 Furnace, x1 Ice Golem. The first icon shows the Inferno Dragon helmet and barrel, not the mechanical Dragon Rider. Local ClashKing data gives 15+18+15 = 48 housing spaces. Hero banners show Queen, King, Warden and Royal Champion. Overall confidence: medium, approximately 80%. Grid/wall topology and most building identities are higher confidence; exact coordinates in the occluded clusters listed below are lower confidence. The single screenshot does not justify claiming a fully exact reconstruction. Exact top tiles of the four hero banners near the Town Hall are less certain because the banners and their pads overlap building artwork; allow approximately one tile. The lower-left Archer Tower at (18,35), Spell Factory at (18,38), and Bomb Tower at (18,41) have tightly packed pads. Their separation is legal, but the Archer Tower position is approximately one tile uncertain. Air Sweepers at (25,11) and (31,17) are partly occluded by huts and walls; their exact positions are approximately one tile uncertain. Facing directions are not encoded. Dark Barracks at (26,1) and Dark Spell Factory at (3,23) are the best visual identifications of the two unusual army-building sprites; their identities warrant another screenshot or an in-game layout link for confirmation. Town Hall (32,8), Hero Hall (37,36), Workshop (4,3), and Eagle Artillery (14,26) have partially concealed footprint edges; allow approximately one tile for exact top-tile placement. 323 wall tiles are transcribed. Two tiles relative to the 325-wall limit are unlocated; they may be occluded or unused. They were not invented. No Hidden Teslas or traps are confidently visible. None were placed. Building levels were not inferred. Digitized from a screenshot; positions about +-1 tile; traps placed by heuristic (not visible in screenshots); built with the user's levels. Hidden Teslas not visible in the screenshot: 5 placed inside the walls at [(30, 8), (13, 32), (41, 28), (11, 12), (27, 33)] (assumed).",
